# Review ownership for the release path.
#
# GitHub consults this file ONLY when evaluating pull request reviews, so on its own
# it blocks nothing. What enforces it is the org ruleset on this branch, which
# requires a pull request and a code owner's approval. Direct pushes to this branch
# are refused by that same rule.
#
# It is read from the branch a PR TARGETS, which is why this file exists separately
# on test and on prod rather than only on the default branch.
#
# Ordinary changes need no approval (the rule asks for zero). Only the paths below
# require one, so day-to-day work on this branch is unaffected.

/.github/ @michaelmarshall
